    "intro_html":  "This is the red stew that sits at the center of Nigerian home cooking, the one that gets spooned over rice at every table and every party. The beef gets boiled first so its stock becomes part of the sauce, then a blended pepper base is fried down until the oil separates and the color goes deep. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
